<title>POLAND: Poland to end zero-duty rapeseed import as planned.</title>
<headline>Poland to end zero-duty rapeseed import as planned.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland will restore a 15 percent customs tariff on rapeseed imports on July 1 as earlier planned, an Agriculture Ministry official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The official told Reuters that there was no preferential rate for rapeseed grown in the European Union.</p>
<p>Poland last November suspended duties on most grains and rapeseed to the end of June 1997 to help keep food prices down. --Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
